    "guardRecommendations": [
      "Require clean dropdown menuDescription field and existing native-generated root. Never regenerate/open/register native cache from addon Lua.",
      "Use original shared local metatable Pick; reject own shadow or tainted shared Pick. Do not depend on a global MenuElementDescriptionProxyMixin.",
      "Require clean selected-entry fields data, responder, isEnabled, canSelect, defaultResponse, and native shared method fields used by Pick.",
      "Require clean Current data.type/sessionID; select original stored data indirectly through native Pick; never pass addon enum/session scalars to native setters.",
      "Original native data/responder is not copied, replaced, hooked or mutated. Matching GetData may inspect safe configuration only, never combat contents.",
      "Explicit user layout/type/setup action may apply; ordinary geometry/events preserve later manual segment overrides. Missing or tainted native cache returns truthful pending/unavailable feedback.",
      "Native OnLoad normally creates clean caches because dropdowns have own shown flag; original New Window responder should initialize newly created windows synchronously.",
      "No direct supported C_DamageMeter type/session/window setter exists in current declarations; native menu route remains separate from rejected private setter experiment."
    ],
